<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Pardo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1834">1834</a>–<a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Manuel Pardo y Lavalle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Pardo was a Peruvian businessman and politician, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/civilista-party">Civilista Party</a>, who was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from 1872 to 1876, the first civilian elected to the office. He sought to use guano revenue for railways, education and productive investment, but his government faced falling guano income and a debt crisis. He was assassinated in 1878 while serving as president of the Senate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-pardo.jpg" alt="Manuel Pardo" width="320" height="468" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ManuelPardo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
